### Loading After Opening
Open the drawer first, and hand the record to `initialValues` once it arrives. It becomes the saved state; fields the user has already changed keep their edits.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const open = ref(false)
const project = ref()

async function edit(id) {
  project.value = undefined
  open.value = true
  project.value = await fetchProject(id)
}
</script>

<template>
  <TxDrawerForm v-model:visible="open" title="Edit project" :initial-values="project" :disabled="!project" @submit="save">
    <template #default="{ model }">…</template>
  </TxDrawerForm>
</template>
```

### Best Practices

- Use it for forms with many fields, forms that scroll, or forms read against the page. For a few fields, use `TxModalForm`.
- Set the drawer's width in `drawerProps.size`. The form's own `size` sizes its controls.
- Drawer forms do not autosave. To save as the user edits, put a `TxForm` with `autosave` in a `TxDrawer`.
- Return a promise from `@submit`. Return `false`, throw, or call `setErrors()`, and the drawer stays open.
- Outside English, pass `submitText`, `cancelText`, `messages.leaveConfirm`, and `drawerProps.closeLabel` to name the close button.

## API Reference

### Props

Every `TxForm` prop except `model` and `autosave` applies too: `rules`, `layout`, `messages`, `persist`, `leaveConfirm`, `readonly` and the rest.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `visible` | `boolean` | required | Shows the drawer. Use with `v-model:visible`. |
| `title` | `string` | `''` | Drawer title. |
| `initialValues` | `FormValues` | - | The values the form opens with. Each open edits a copy, so the parent's values change only when the parent changes them. |
| `submitText` | `string` | `'Save'` | Text of the submit button. |
| `cancelText` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Text of the cancel button. |
| `drawerProps` | `Record<string, unknown>` | - | Any other `TxDrawer` prop, such as `size` or `direction`. Closing is asked of the form, not of `beforeClose`. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `update:visible` | `(value: boolean)` | The drawer opens or closes. |
| `submit` | `(values: FormValues, event?: Event)` | Called once every check passes. The drawer stays open until a returned promise settles. |
| `submit-success` | `(values: FormValues)` | The submit went through; the drawer closes next. |
| `validate` | `(valid: boolean)` | As on `TxForm`. |
| `persist-error` | `(error: unknown)` | As on `TxForm`. |

### Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `default` | `{ model, dirty, valid, submitting, submitted, errors, rootError }` | The form items. `model` is the copy this open edits. |
| `footer` | `{ formId, submitting, cancel }` | Replaces the cancel and submit buttons. Point the submit button at the form with `:form="formId"`. |

### Exposed Methods

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `form` | `TxForm \| null` | The form inside, with every `TxForm` method; `null` until the drawer first opens. |
| `cancel` | `() => Promise<void>` | Closes as Cancel does: the form first asks about changes it would lose. |

## Overview

- Each open builds `model` from a copy of `initialValues` and makes it the baseline, so edits left at closing never carry over to the next open.
- When `initialValues` changes while the drawer is open, it becomes the saved state: untouched fields take the new values, and fields the user changed keep their edits.
- Escape, the mask, the close button and Cancel all go through the form's `confirmLeave()`, which asks only about changes no draft holds. A running submit cannot be closed.
- After its first open the drawer keeps its content, and the form with it. Closed, it has nothing left to lose, so reloading the page does not ask.
- A submit that goes through emits `submit-success`, then closes.

## Technologies

- Built from `TxDrawer` and `TxForm`, with `beforeClose` wired to the form's `confirmLeave()`. Opening, copying and closing share `form/src/use-overlay-form.ts` with `TxModalForm`.
- The footer sits outside the `<form>`, and the submit button reaches it through `form`: Enter in a field and a click make the same submit.
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/drawer-form/`.

